## Actual RX engine verification

The new DLL was subsequently exercised by the actual RX executable,
`D:/RX/Main/UE5/Engine/Binaries/Win64/UnrealEditor-Cmd.exe`, in an isolated
content-only harness at `MCPGameProject/Saved/Tests/RXInspector`. The harness
uses a copy of the new plugin binaries, the existing RX deployment's module
manifest (RX BuildId), and the development project's content via a junction.
It uses D3D12/SM6 and disables PlasticSourceControl/N10XSourceCodeAccess,
matching the two disabled plugins in the RX project. The running user's RX
project and plugin files were not replaced or restarted.

`InspectorActualRXTests.log` confirms engine `5.6.1-0+++depot+Program` and
`engine access=RX (RX reflected marker=true, requested=Auto)`. All eight native
inspector tests passed, including real rendered mesh/animation/Niagara,
animation time advancement, preview release, and result-window lifecycle.
The RX screenshots were visually inspected under
`Saved/Tests/RXInspector/Saved/Logs/InspectorHost*Preview.png`.

This is actual RX engine binary coverage, not an override on stock UE. It is
still an isolated harness: the deployed RX project's gameplay-specific
double-click/end-PIE/re-selection flow awaits DLL replacement and restart.
The log also contains three generic `LogAutomationTest: Condition failed`
messages during engine startup, before test execution; none was attributed to
an inspector test, and the inspector suite and process completed successfully.

## RX live-preview camera controls

The host `UViewport` preview now receives navigation through its owning Slate
wrapper. Camera transforms use host exports; the plugin does not allocate an
editor viewport client, access its private layout, or use SceneCapture.

| Input | Action |
| --- | --- |
| Alt + LMB drag | Orbit around the preview target |
| MMB drag / Alt + MMB drag / LMB + RMB drag | Pan |
| Alt + RMB drag / Alt + LMB + MMB drag | Dolly |
| Wheel | Dolly towards/away from the target |
| RMB drag / LMB drag | Orbit around the current asset bounds center, including after pan/movement |
| RMB + WASD / arrow keys | Fly forward/back/left/right |
| RMB + QE / PageDown/PageUp | Move down/up in world space |
| RMB + R | Move up along the camera's vertical axis |
| Shift while flying | Four-times movement speed |
| RMB + wheel | Adjust flight speed (0.05x–32x) |
| F (also while RMB is held) / Frame button | Center and tightly fit the asset AABB, retaining the viewing angle |
| Auto rotate checkbox | Toggle mesh rotation |
| Escape during a drag | Release camera input |

Manual navigation disables automatic framing until Frame/F or a new asset
selection, so Niagara bounds updates cannot overwrite the user's camera.
Framing projects all eight AABB corners with a 2% edge margin and near-clip
clearance. RX uses the host's exported view-projection matrix to respect its
actual FOV and axis constraint. Focus loss, asset changes and teardown clear navigation state. The
destructor avoids querying Slate capture after the last shared reference dies.
Standard UE uses its editor viewport with the same AABB fitting, F shortcut,
and asset-centered LMB/RMB rotation; its editor FOV-axis settings are respected.

This restores movement, rotation, orbit, pan, distance zoom and speed controls.
It does not reproduce C/Z optical FOV changes: UE 5.6 `UViewport` has no public
FOV setter. Editor user-specific inversion/sensitivity settings are also not
mirrored by this wrapper.

Camera checkpoint (2026-09-06): UE 5.6.1 editor build succeeded, and all nine
inspector tests passed in the actual RX D3D12/SM6 harness with automatic RX
detection. The new `CameraInput` test routes native Slate mouse/key events and
checks orbit, pan, look, flight, zoom, speed, and capture/high-precision release
on mouse-up, focus loss and asset removal. Fixtures use Slate's actual cursor
pointer index and send matching release events. Existing rendering and window
lifecycle tests also passed; rendered screenshots were visually inspected.
The initial teardown assertion was fixed by guarding shared-instance lifetime.
Logs: `InspectorCameraBuild.log` and `InspectorCameraRXTests.log` under
`MCPGameProject/Saved/Logs/`. The RX harness is still isolated; the primary RX
project's installed DLL has not been replaced by this verification.
The final full offline profile passed all 41 entries (`InspectorCameraFull.log`);
